// "L target alias" link in /usr/share/zoneinfo/tzdata.zi mapped to its target's country, so legacy names browsers
// still report (Asia/Calcutta, Europe/Kiev, US/Eastern, Japan, ...) resolve too. A few links whose target is now in
// another country are pinned to the country the name means (Iceland → IS, Pacific/Truk → FM, ...). UTC, Etc/* and
// non-geographic names (EST, CET, ...) are left out. Format: per country, space-separated groups of
// "Region/name,name,..." sharing the text up to the first slash; a group with no slash is a whole zone name.
